  "id": "COMPOUND:20312 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "The compound [(1S,2S,6R,10S,11R,12R,13S,14R,15R)-13-acetyloxy-1,6-dihydroxy-8,12-bis(hydroxymethyl)-4,12,15-trimethyl-5,9-dioxo-14-tetracyclo[8.5.0.02,6.011,13]pentadeca-3,7-dienyl] hexadecanoate] is implicated in the activation of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through multiple pathways. It is directly targeted by Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn is a target of Dendridine A and Serpentine. These intermediates collectively establish a chain of interactions leading to the activation of the kinase. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of the kinase through its interaction with downstream targets, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The strength of the evidence is moderate, with consistent scores across different paths, but the complexity of the pathway and the lack of direct experimental validation may introduce some uncertainty.",
